  "steps": [
    "Pound the chicken between sheets of plastic wrap to an even 1-inch thickness and season with the salt and pepper.",
    "Heat the olive oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat. Cook the chicken 5-6 minutes per side, until browned and 165°F inside. Move to a plate and cover loosely with foil.",
    "Add the butter and garlic to the same pan and cook until fragrant, about 30 seconds.",
    "Pour in the wine and scrape up the browned bits. Simmer until reduced by half, about 3 minutes.",
    "Whisk in the cream, broth, soy sauce, Dijon, and thyme and simmer 2-4 minutes, until slightly thickened.",
    "Return the chicken and its juices to the pan and cook until heated through, about 2 minutes. Spoon the sauce over to serve."
